# T6i review item 2: a STUDIO pattern edit still reaches LIVE after a reboot, and a key assignment
# made in LIVE survives it. The song's record carries the project's pattern hash; the clips are kept
# in step with the project at save time, and a boot (or a LIVE entry) whose hash differs rebuilds
# them, keeping the key map.
wait 300
expect songloaded 0
# a key assignment in LIVE
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 20
expect mode 1
assignkey 0 12
expect keyclip0 12
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 20
expect mode 0
# save (stopped): project and song
tap SAVE
expect songsaves 1
expect songdirty 0
# a STUDIO pattern edit, saved, then a reboot
tapkey w0
expect hit0.0.0 1
tap SAVE
expect songsaves 2
reboot
# the edit is in the stored song (clip 0 is a drum clip now) and the key map survived
expect songloaded 1
expect songdirty 0
expect keyclip0 12
expect liveused0 1
# and LIVE plays it
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 20
expect mode 1
expect liveused0 1
